          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Ruth’s tropical fish are breeding at a rate of 8 new fry every 2 days per female fish.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If Ruth has a total of 9 female fish, then how long will it take them to birth a total of 90 new fry?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$2.5$ days.",
      "worked": "For each female fish, $8\\div2=4$ new fry per day.\n\nFor 9 female fish, $9\\times4=36$ new fry per day.\n\nLet $x$ be the time in days. Using equivalent rates and taking reciprocals:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{36}{1}&=\\frac{90}{x}\\\\\\frac{1}{36}&=\\frac{x}{90}\\\\90\\times\\frac{1}{36}&=x\\\\x&=2.5\\end{align*}$$\n\nIt takes $2.5$ days.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 56
  },
